WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.500
Every time you 
smoke a cigarette,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.500
toxic gases pass into your lungs, 
then into your bloodstream,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.000
where they spread to 
every organ in your body.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.500
A cigarette is made 
using the tobacco leaf,

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.900
which contains nicotine 
and a variety of other compounds.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.500
As the tobacco and 
compounds burn,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.210
they release thousands of 
dangerous chemicals, including

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.000
over forty known 
to cause cancer.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Cigarette smoke contains the poisonous gases 
carbon monoxide and nitrogen oxide,

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
as well as trace amounts of 
cancer-causing radioactive particles.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:11.000
All forms of tobacco are dangerous, including cigars, pipes, and smokeless tobacco, such as chewing tobacco and snuff.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Nicotine is an addictive chemical in tobacco.
After you inhale tobacco smoke,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.500
nicotine flows through the bloodstream to
your brain, where it induces a pleasurable feeling.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.700
When you repeatedly expose your brain to nicotine,

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:34.000
it becomes desensitized,making you crave
 more and more nicotine just to feel normal.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Smoking causes death. People who smoke typically die 
at an earlier age than non-smokers.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:53.000
In fact, 1 of every 5 deaths in the United States 
is linked to cigarette smoking.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.300
If you smoke, your risk for major health problems

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:03.000
increases dramatically, including:
heart disease, heart attack, stroke,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:11.200
lung cancer, and death from 
chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:25.450
Smoking causes cardiovascular disease.
When nicotine flows through your adrenal glands,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:32.760
it stimulates the release of epinephrine,
a hormone that raises your blood pressure.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:41.000
In addition, nicotine and carbon monoxide
can damage the lining of the inner walls in your arteries.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.700
Fatty deposits, called plaque, can build up

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:52.349
at these injury sites and become large enough
to narrow the arteries and severely reduce

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:59.269
blood flow, resulting in a condition 
called atherosclerosis.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:06.269
In coronary artery disease, atherosclerosis
narrows the arteries that supply the heart,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:14.000
which reduces the supply of oxygen to your
heart muscle, increasing your risk for a heart attack.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.500
Smoking also raises your risk for blood clots

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:23.709
because it causes platelets in your blood
to clump together.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:27.379
Smoking increases your risk for 
peripheral vascular disease,

00:03:27.379 --> 00:03:34.379
in which atherosclerotic plaques block the
large arteries in your arms and legs.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.669
Smoking can also cause an 
abdominal aortic aneurysm,

00:03:38.669 --> 00:03:45.600
which is a swelling or weakening of your aorta
where it runs through your abdomen.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:58.000
Smoking damages two main parts of your lungs:
your airways, also called bronchial tubes,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.000
and small air sacs called alveoli.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:08.000
With each breath, air travels down 
your windpipe, called the trachea,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.019
and enters your lungs through your bronchial tubes.

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:17.000
Air then moves into 
thousands of tiny alveoli,

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.000
where oxygen from the air 
moves into your bloodstream

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:29.000
and the waste product carbon dioxide 
moves out of your bloodstream.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.500
Tiny hair-like projections, called cilia,

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:38.500
line your bronchial tubes and sweep harmful
substances out of your lungs.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:44.000
Cigarette smoke irritates the lining of your
bronchial tubes,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.900
causing them to swell and make mucus.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Cigarette smoke also slows 
the movement of your cilia,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:57.000
causing some of the smoke 
and mucus to stay in your lungs.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.000
While you are sleeping, 
some of the cilia recover

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:07.800
and start pushing more pollutants
and mucus out of your lungs.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:13.000
When you wake up, your body attempts to expel
this material by coughing repeatedly,

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.000
a condition known as 
smoker's cough.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.000
Over time, chronic bronchitis develops 
as your cilia stop working,

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.500
your airways become clogged with scars and mucus, 
and breathing becomes difficult.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:33.000
Your lungs are now more vulnerable to further disease.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.090
Cigarette smoke also 
damages your alveoli,

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:42.500
making it harder for oxygen and 
carbon dioxide to exchange with your blood.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:48.630
Over time, so little oxygen can reach your
blood that you may develop emphysema,

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:53.000
a condition in which you must gasp for every
breath and wear an oxygen tube

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:57.000
under your nose 
in order to breathe.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Chronic bronchitis and emphysema 
are collectively called

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.500
chronic obstructive pulmonary disease,
or COPD.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:12.740
COPD is a gradual loss of the ability to breathe
for which there is no cure.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:25.200
Cigarette smoke contains at least 40 cancer-causing
substances, called carcinogens, including

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:32.260
cyanide, formaldehyde, 
benzene, and ammonia.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:39.000
In your body, healthy cells grow, 
make new cells, then die.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:45.000
Genetic material inside each cell, 
called DNA, directs this process.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:54.000
If you smoke, toxic chemicals 
can damage the DNA in your healthy cells.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.000
As a result, your damaged cells 
create new unhealthy cells,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:05.000
which grow out of control 
and may spread to other parts of your body.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:08.500
The most common cancer 
in the world is lung cancer,

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.500
with over a million new cases 
diagnosed every year.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:21.500
Harmful chemicals in cigarettes can cause
cancer in other parts of your body, such as:

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:28.500
in the blood and bone marrow, 
mouth, larynx, throat,

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:36.000
esophagus, stomach, 
pancreas, kidney,

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.000
bladder, uterus, and cervix.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:53.000
Smoking can cause infertility 
in both men and women.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:57.600
If a woman is pregnant and 
smokes during pregnancy,

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:03.600
she exposes her baby to the cigarette's poisonous
chemicals, causing a greater risk of:

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:10.000
low birth weight, miscarriage, 
preterm delivery, stillbirth,

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.000
infant death, and 
sudden infant death syndrome.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Smoking is also dangerous 
if a mother is breastfeeding.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.900
Nicotine passes to the baby 
through breast milk,

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:35.900
and can cause restlessness, rapid heartbeat,
vomiting, interrupted sleep, or diarrhea.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:41.700
Other health effects of smoking 
include low bone density

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.100
and increased risk for hip 
fracture among women;

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:49.000
gum disease, often leading 
to tooth loss and surgery;

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.100
immune system dysfunction 
and delayed wound healing;

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.100
and sexual impotence in men.

